    <!-- Educational capsules -->
    <string name="capsule_seer_title">SEER: cooling with fewer watts</string>
    <string name="capsule_seer_body">A high SEER delivers the same cooling with less electricity. It is the number that really moves your bill, not just the BTU/h.</string>
    <string name="capsule_myth_title">The 17 °C myth</string>
    <string name="capsule_myth_body">Each degree below 24 °C costs about 6 %% more. The room feels the same with a ceiling fan; the compressor does not need to fight the thermostat.</string>
    <string name="capsule_small_title">The small AC trap</string>
    <string name="capsule_small_body">An undersized unit runs at 100 %% without modulating, uses more, and wears out sooner. Buy the tier that covers the real area.</string>
    <string name="capsule_protector_title">Inverter protector and joules</string>
    <string name="capsule_protector_body">On Inverter the protector goes on the direct line (terminals): AVTEK SPC-PEBAS-B230 at 2,100 J or Forza FVP-6630B at 880 J. Without it, a surge burns the board.</string>
    <string name="capsule_dry_title">Dry Mode vs. dehumidifier</string>
    <string name="capsule_dry_body">Dry Mode lowers humidity without forcing the compressor like cooling does. A dehumidifier helps, but it consumes separately and you must empty its tank.</string>

